ror_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376104, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013jJYQRDxiWd9bYqeAhwyBh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 379914, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The problem:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed, since it expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. The advisory lookup didn't recognise \"FIN-212\", so I worked from the test and the docstring.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Li9tujZYMxdMPjyMazB9Pd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BHeLYHvMufbyx2tczP77uq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0122DKW3ciKmHvet67CYKhD2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LcisFi7n3pfhLWsg4gfTzK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_us